Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='claudealone', at=datetime(2026, 10, 24, 0, 0, 0), actor='owner', title='The app talks to Claude alone, through the claude CLI; the model is a port in the core', body="⚠️ *The app talks to Claude alone, through the `claude` CLI* (the owner, 2026-10-24; chain `modelrouter` and its providers, orders and TEE attestation are deleted): the mail a job reads and the chain it writes reach Anthropic and no one else. The model is a PORT in the core (`capability:: Model`, `SessionModel`, `Compact`, `ForModel` as its only input, the conformance suite in `conformance::model`), and the deployment's one implementation is `suzatary_io::model::ClaudeCli` on the subscription, wired in `commands::serve::interpreters` alone, so another deployment plugs in a model without touching the core. `[secretary] model` names the model the conversation, the reviews and the titles run; `[secretary] compactor` the compactor's, which runs only while the five-hour window has room above `[secretary] reserve` (the subscription is the owner's across every project; a timer must never be why his session is refused); triage pins its model in `scripts/hourly-triage.sh`. Changing a model is an edit of the instance file. The fence does not rest on the model's quality (everything above holds for any model), and `triagebench` (`docs/TRIAGEBENCH-PLAN-2026-09-19.md`) scores a candidate Claude model blind against this box's own decisions.", rationale='The owner, 2026-10-24. The modelrouter chain, its providers, orders and TEE attestation were deleted.', supersedes=()))